    "b-30-runtime-decision-role-neutral-8": {
      "id": "b-30-runtime-decision-role-neutral-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — The runtime is role-neutral: prompt building and output parsing belong to the owning agent slice, with generic JSON salvage as the only parsing the runtime performs. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — rejected role-specific branches in shared runtime code; role knowledge in the runtime couples every agent to every other agent's changes. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime",
              "label": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", including any future runtime helper."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-30-runtime-decision-shared-builders-9": {
      "id": "b-30-runtime-decision-shared-builders-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — Dry-run and live mode share the same prompt builders, and every rendered prompt and context packet persists as an artifact beside agent output. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — rejected a separate preview path; drift between what previews show and what agents receive is a regression class this rule removes. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime/runtime",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime/runtime",
              "label": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime/runtime"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and every current or future invocation path."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-30-runtime-decision-bridge-10": {
      "id": "b-30-runtime-decision-bridge-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — Live DB-backed spawns go through the server kernel bridge with a kernel context resolver; paths that cannot inject kernel context must compose the same rendered context packet into the prompt instead. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — rejected divergent fallback prompts; audit artifacts, previews, and live sessions must expose the same injected input. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/kernel/bridge",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/kernel/bridge",
              "label": "apps/server/src/infrastructure/kernel/bridge"
            }
          }
        },
